          <Pad Id="BUkroTe82qpPk2n8aFqJZt" Bounds="85,850,840,179" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- All QtTextures of a frame render together at the start of Stride's draw, on a Qt render thread: every texture is ready in the same frame. With the environment variable VLQT_OFFSCREEN_THREAD=0 (set before vvvv starts) they render on the main thread, for diagnosis.&#xD;&#xA;- Every QtTexture holds a texture of its Size in pixels: many large ones cost GPU memory.&#xD;&#xA;- QtTexture outputs premultiplied alpha. AlphaBlend expects straight alpha: it multiplies RGB by alpha a second time and makes half-transparent parts too dark. Where straight alpha is needed, unpremultiply the texture first (RGB divided by alpha).&#xD;&#xA;- Windows only (Direct3D 11). QtTexture is Experimental: pins and behavior may still change.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
